[{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00ba2","question":"In an amplitude modulated signal, the amplitude of the carrier wave will:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad448","isCorrect":false,"choice":"remain constant, and the frequency will vary according to the amplitude of the modulating signal"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad449","isCorrect":true,"choice":"vary according to the amplitude of the modulating signal"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"vary according to the frequency of the modulating signal"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00bad","question":"As a radio signal increases in frequency, ionospheric refraction … and atmospheric attenuation…","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"decreases; decreases"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44c","isCorrect":true,"choice":"increases; decreases"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"increases; increases"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00baa","question":"The frequency corresponding to a wavelength of 3.5 cm is:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"857 MHz"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad44f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"85.7 MHz"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad450","isCorrect":true,"choice":"8.57 GHz"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00ba5","question":"Around a radiating transmitter aerial there is:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad451","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a magnetic field"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad452","isCorrect":false,"choice":"an electrical field"},{"_