ce Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00ba3","question":"To establish and maintain effective HF communications the frequency used at a given range:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad45d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"should remain constant"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad45e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"should only be varied by season, decreased in summer and increased in winter"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad45f","isCorrect":true,"choice":"should be decreased at night"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00ba8","question":"For a given HF frequency skip distance will normally:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad460","isCorrect":false,"choice":"be greater by day than by night"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad461","isCorrect":true,"choice":"be greater by night than by day"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad462","isCorrect":false,"choice":"be less by night than by day"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00ba6","question":"The rate of attenuation of a radio wave which occurs when the wave travels close to the Earths surface.","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad463","isCorrect":false,"choice":"decreases as the frequency of the wave increases, and is greater over the land than the sea"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad464","isCorrect":true,"choice":"increases as the frequency of the wave increases, and is greater over the land than the sea"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad465","isCorrect":false,"choice":"decreases as the frequency of the wave increases, and is greater over the than the land"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00bab","question":"In sky wave propagation the distance between the end of the surface wave and the first returning sky wave is called the:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad466","isCorrect":false,"choice":"maximum usable range"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad467","isCorrect":true,"choice":"dead space"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad468","isCorrect":false,"choice":"skip distance"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00bac","question":"A frequency of 295 KHz would be described as:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad469","isCorrect":true,"choice":"LF"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"short wave"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"MF"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5bd715cc08c3f00bae","question":"Sky waves are not likely to occur by day or night in whihc of the following frequency bands:","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46c","isCorrect":true,"choice":"VHF"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"HF"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"MF"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d5dd715cc08c3f00bb6","question":"When is fading in the medium frequency band most likely to occur","choices":[{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad46f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"During the day with ground and sky waves"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad470","isCorrect":true,"choice":"During rainy days"},{"_id":"693e819d6a1995dddc7ad471","isCorrect":false,"choice":"During rainy nights"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Navigation","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Basic Radio Theory"},{"image":"","difficulty":"